{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"ls -la /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1 && rg -n \\\"\\\" /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1 -g '*'\"","aggregated_output":"total 48\ndrwxrwxr-x+ 2 xd xd  4096 May 26 10:23 .\ndrwxrwxr-x+ 7 xd xd  4096 May 26 10:15 ..\n-rw-rw-r--+ 1 xd xd  8479 May 26 10:23 des.md\n-rw-rw-r--+ 1 xd xd   280 May 26 10:15 ids.txt\n-rw-rw-r--+ 1 xd xd 23229 May 26 10:15 prompt.md\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:1:你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:2:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:3:每个参考题描述包含：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:4:- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:5:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:6:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:7:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:8:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:9:参考题目如下：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:10:<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"5dbc8537\" lines=\"10-23\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:11:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:12:Fill rectangular cavities in a template shape by placing source sprites into matching holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:13:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:14:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:15:- bg = most common color. A dominant \"base\" color forms a large frame/template with rectangular gaps.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:16:- Small colored sprites sit outside the template region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:17:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:18:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:19:- The base color (largest connected component excluding bg) defines the template bbox.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:20:- Each rectangular hole inside the template matches exactly one outside sprite by size.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:21:- Place each sprite into its matching cavity; output is the filled template bbox.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:22:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:23:Key insight: Sprite bounding boxes match cavity dimensions exactly — it's a jigsaw-fit puzzle where each piece has a unique slot.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:24:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:25:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:26:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:27:<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"195c6913\" lines=\"37-52\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:28:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:29:Simulate particles along a path with alternating turn direction at collisions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:30:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:31:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:32:- Top-left: 2x2 monochrome blocks define a repeating color cycle (left-to-right).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:33:- Isolated single pixels of a cycle color: start markers adjacent to the path.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:34:- A 2x2 monochrome block of a distinct color: end marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:35:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:36:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:37:- Each start marker launches a particle moving straight, painting cycle colors in order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:38:- On hitting a boundary, paint that cell with the end color and turn 90°.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:39:- Turn direction alternates: odd collisions → left (CCW), even → right (CW).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:40:- If the scheduled turn is blocked, the particle stops.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:41:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:42:Key insight: The alternating left/right turn rule is the core mechanism; without it the path would be trivial.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:43:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:44:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:45:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:46:<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"271d71e2\" lines=\"9-22\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:47:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:48:Move bordered containers toward same-colored destination markers, charging gray cells to orange.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:49:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:50:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:51:- bg = 6 (magenta). Black-bordered (0) rectangles with gray (5) / orange (7) interiors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:52:- A head sprite (9) sits adjacent to one container edge; a matching destination sprite lies along the movement axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:53:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:54:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:55:- Each container translates toward its destination along the head-to-dest axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:56:- Steps = min(head-to-dest distance, number of gray interior cells).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:57:- Gray cells become orange from the head-facing side inward, one per step.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:58:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:59:Key insight: Gray cell count caps movement — a container stops short if it runs out of gray cells to charge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:60:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:61:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:62:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:63:<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8f215267\" lines=\"7-21\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:64:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:65:Count same-color patterns per frame and represent the tally as dots inside.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:66:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:67:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:68:- bg = most common color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:69:- Hollow rectangular frames in various colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:70:- Small monochrome pattern sprites scattered outside frames.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:71:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:72:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:73:- Remove all small patterns from the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:74:- For each frame of color C, count how many patterns share color C.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:75:- Draw that many dots along the frame's center row, spaced by 2, starting from the right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:76:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:77:Key insight: Frames act as tally displays — scattered same-color patterns are \"absorbed\" and their count is shown as interior dots.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:78:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:79:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:80:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:81:<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"142ca369\" lines=\"6-19\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:82:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:83:Trace diagonal rays from triangular arrows, reflecting off colored wall pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:84:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:85:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:86:- bg grid with monochrome 3-pixel L-shaped \"arrows\" (2x2 bbox missing one corner) and scattered colored wall pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:87:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:88:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:89:- Each arrow fires a ray diagonally away from its missing corner, painting bg cells in its color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:90:- A head-on wall hit reverses both axes; a side-touch wall hit flips the touched axis only.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:91:- On any bounce the ray adopts the wall's color and recolors the contact cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:92:- Ray stops when it exits the grid or reaches another arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:93:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:94:Key insight: Two distinct reflection types (corner vs side-touch) plus color inheritance at each bounce drive the path geometry.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:95:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:96:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:97:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:98:<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"da515329\" lines=\"11-24\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:99:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:100:Grow four clockwise spiral wall paths from the tips of a teal cross.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:101:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:102:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:103:- bg = 0 (black). A single teal (8) cross centered in the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:104:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:105:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:106:- Each arm tip launches a \"turtle\" heading 90° right of its outward direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:107:- Movement priority: turn right > go straight > turn left (left only if not on border).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:108:- Normal step = 2 cells; step right after a turn = 1 cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:109:- Each new cell must have a 1-cell orthogonal gap from all existing walls except the predecessor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:110:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:111:Key insight: The right-turn preference plus alternating 2/1 step lengths creates self-avoiding spirals that tile the grid with uniform spacing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:112:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:113:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:114:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:115:<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"45a5af55\" lines=\"5-18\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:116:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:117:Build nested square frames from a stack of horizontal color stripes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:118:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:119:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:120:- Full-width horizontal stripes of distinct non-bg colors, stacked vertically.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:121:- Each stripe has uniform color and variable height (1-4 rows).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:122:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:123:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:124:- Read stripes bottom to top.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:125:- Bottom stripe becomes the center solid square with side length = stripe height.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:126:- Each subsequent stripe wraps the current shape with a square frame of thickness = stripe height, in that stripe's color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:127:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:128:Key insight: Stripe height doubles as both frame thickness and (for the innermost) center-square side length; output dimensions are fully determined by the stripe heights.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:129:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:130:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:131:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:132:<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"6e453dd6\" lines=\"39-52\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:133:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:134:Slide black shapes rightward to a grey separator, then shoot red rays from enclosed holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:135:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:136:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:137:- A vertical grey (5) separator column divides the grid into left and right halves.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:138:- Black shapes sit on the left side against a background color (bg).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:139:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:140:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:141:- Translate each black connected component rightward until its right edge is flush with the separator.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:142:- After sliding, find enclosed bg regions (holes) within the black shapes that touch the column just left of the separator.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:143:- For each row spanned by such a hole, emit a red ray across the entire right half of the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:144:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:145:Key insight: Only holes adjacent to the separator trigger rays — the sliding creates enclosures that act as \"nozzles\" projecting rightward.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:146:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:147:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:148:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:149:<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"9385bd28\" lines=\"71-87\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:150:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:151:Fill rectangles between diagonal marker pairs using a color legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:152:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:153:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:154:- bg grid with a vertical legend at the bottom-left: each row is a (marker_color, fill_color) pair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:155:- Scattered L-shaped corner markers of each marker color define opposite corners of axis-aligned rectangles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:156:- Some markers are solid 2×2 blocks instead of corner pairs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:157:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:158:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:159:- Read legend bottom-to-top; for each entry find all pixels of that marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:160:- Determine which two bbox corners carry L-shaped anchors — the *other* diagonal defines the fill region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:161:- Fill the diamond (all shortest-path cells between those two corners) with the legend's fill color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:162:- Solid 2×2 marker blocks are simply recolored to the fill color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:163:- Later legend entries are protected from earlier fills.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:164:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:165:Key insight: The L-shaped anchors sit on the marker diagonal; the fill goes on the opposite diagonal of the bounding box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:166:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:167:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:168:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:169:<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"f560132c\" lines=\"259-273\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:170:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:171:Assemble scattered jigsaw pieces into a rectangle, recoloring each by a legend sprite's color map.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:172:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:173:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:174:- bg = most common color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:175:- Several monochrome non-bg sprites (the \"pieces\"), scattered across the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:176:- One sprite is the legend: it contains a multi-color k×k patch (typically 2×2) encoding output colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:177:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:178:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:179:- Tile all pieces (rotations/reflections allowed) into a tight rectangle with no gaps.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:180:- The legend's k×k color patch defines a spatial color map over the rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:181:- Each piece is recolored to the legend-map color corresponding to its position in the assembled rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:182:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:183:Key insight: The legend piece doubles as both a jigsaw piece and a color key — its internal k×k palette assigns colors by spatial quadrant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:184:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:185:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:186:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:187:<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"58490d8a\" lines=\"9-21\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:188:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:189:Count colored objects and record tallies inside a legend box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:190:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:191:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:192:- A black rectangular legend box with key-color pixels in its leftmost non-black column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:193:- Outside the box, distinct objects of each key color are scattered across the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:194:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:195:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:196:- For each key color, count separate same-colored objects outside the legend box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:197:- Output the legend box repainted: each key row gets one dot per object, spaced every other cell rightward from the key pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:198:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:199:Key insight: The legend is both the color index and the output canvas — object counts become dot sequences on the matching row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:200:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:201:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:202:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:203:<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"62593bfd\" lines=\"32-46\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:204:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:205:Sort objects to top or bottom edge by whether their shape (up to rotation/flip) is shared.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:206:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:207:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:208:- bg = most common color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:209:- Several multicolor connected components (8-connected) scattered across the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:210:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:211:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:212:- Compute each object's canonical shape (binary mask, invariant to rotation and flip).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:213:- Objects whose shape appears in two or more components → translate to TOP edge (row 0).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:214:- Objects whose shape is unique → translate to BOTTOM edge (row H−h).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:215:- Horizontal position (left column) is preserved; only vertical translation changes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:216:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:217:Key insight: The sorting criterion is shape frequency (rotation-invariant), not area — duplicated shapes go up, unique shapes go down.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:218:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:219:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:220:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:221:<reference_puzzle index=\"13\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"80a900e0\" lines=\"69-82\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:222:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:223:Extend diagonal rays outward from outer-border segments adjacent to diamond shapes on a checkerboard.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:224:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:225:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:226:- Checkerboard bg (two most common colors).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:227:- Hollow diamond outlines (8-pixel) in a non-bg color (inner border).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:228:- Short diagonal line segments in another non-bg color adjacent to each diamond edge (outer border).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:229:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:230:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:231:- For each outer-border segment, determine the outward direction (perpendicular to the segment, away from the diamond).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:232:- From each endpoint of the segment, cast a diagonal ray outward, painting over bg pixels with the segment's color until hitting a non-bg pixel or the grid edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:233:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:234:Key insight: Rays emit only from the two endpoints of each outer-border segment, not every pixel, and travel diagonally away from the diamond.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:235:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:236:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:237:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:238:<reference_puzzle index=\"14\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"269e22fb\" lines=\"46-60\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:239:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:240:Complete a visible crop into the shared 20x20 binary motif in its matching orientation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:241:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:242:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:243:- The grid is a two-color rectangular crop of one rotation/reflection of the same 20x20 motif.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:244:- One color is the motif foreground and the other color is the motif background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:245:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:246:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:247:- Try each input color as the foreground mask.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:248:- Match that mask against every possible window in every dihedral orientation of the motif.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:249:- Repaint the uniquely matched full 20x20 motif with the matched foreground/background colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:250:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:251:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:252:- The examples are partial windows of one canonical binary pattern; the local crop is distinctive enough to identify the full orientation and offset.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:253:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:254:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:255:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:256:<reference_puzzle index=\"15\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"4c3d4a41\" lines=\"15-28\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:257:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:258:Fit a grey bar into a grey frame by aligning projections with colored columns, then stack colors above.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:259:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:260:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:261:- bg, a grey structural color forming two components: a large rectangular frame (slot) and a smaller bar with upward projections.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:262:- Colored pixels inside the slot mark target columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:263:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:264:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:265:- Move the bar upward into the slot so its bottom edge sits one cell above the slot's interior bottom.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:266:- Shift it horizontally so the bar's upward projections align column-wise with the colored pixels in the slot.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:267:- Stack the colored pixels immediately above the bar projections in each column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:268:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:269:Key insight: The bar's projections act as keys that must align with the colored-column \"locks\" in the slot.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:270:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:271:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:272:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:273:<reference_puzzle index=\"16\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"e12f9a14\" lines=\"138-152\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:274:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:275:Emit diagonal beams from framed 2x2 blocks through frame gaps; beams interact on collision.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:276:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:277:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:278:- bg = most common color. Wall color (e.g. green) forms 4x4 frames around 2x2 monochrome blocks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:279:- Each frame has one or more gap pixels where the wall is missing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:280:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:281:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:282:- Each gap emits a beam of the inner block's color, traveling diagonally outward (direction set by gap position relative to the block).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:283:- Beams paint every cell they cross until they hit the grid edge or collide.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:284:- 90° collision: both beams turn 45° toward their bisector direction; the intersection cell is left blank (1-pixel gap).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:285:- 45° collision: beams merge into a zigzag (alternating cardinal + diagonal steps) with no gap at the meeting point.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:286:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:287:Key insight: Two distinct collision rules — 90° produces a gap and single-pixel diagonal lines; 45° produces no gap and thicker zigzag bands.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:288:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:289:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:290:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:291:<reference_puzzle index=\"17\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"221dfab4\" lines=\"6-19\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:292:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:293:Propagate a repeating striped pattern from a yellow border segment toward the opposite edge, recoloring foreground objects on certain stripes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:294:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:295:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:296:- bg = most common color. Foreground blobs of another color scattered in the interior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:297:- A short yellow (4) segment sits on one border edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:298:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:299:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:300:- From the yellow segment, march toward the opposite edge in steps of 2 cells, cycling colors Y, Y, G (4, 4, 3). The 1-cell gap between stripes is forced to bg.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:301:- Yellow stripes paint only within the segment's span.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:302:- Green stripes additionally recolor all non-bg pixels across the entire row/column to green.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:303:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:304:Key insight: Green stripes act as a \"flood\" that recolors existing objects on the full row/column, while yellow stripes are confined to the segment span.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:305:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:306:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:307:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:308:<reference_puzzle index=\"18\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"36a08778\" lines=\"8-21\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:309:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:310:Simulate water falling from top-edge sources, pooling on shelves, and cascading off edges.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:311:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:312:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:313:- bg = most common color; water = rarest non-bg; shelf = other non-bg.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:314:- Sources: water clusters touching top row. Shelves: horizontal segments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:315:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:316:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:317:- Water falls down from sources, painting bg cells as water.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:318:- On hitting a shelf, it spreads across the shelf span plus one cell past each end.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:319:- From those overflow positions, water resumes falling independently.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:320:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:321:Key insight: Each shelf splits a stream into two at its edges, creating a branching waterfall tree.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:322:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:323:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:324:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:325:<reference_puzzle index=\"19\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"e87109e9\" lines=\"68-83\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:326:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:327:Emit four teal beams from a square, turning at colored obstacles per a legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:328:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:329:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:330:- Top band: grey (5) legend with colored vertical bars in cells; bar position (left or right) encodes turn direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:331:- Below: main grid with bg, a solid teal (8) square, and colored obstacle blocks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:332:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:333:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:334:- Remove the legend from the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:335:- From the teal square, shoot a beam in each cardinal direction (as a sliding copy of the square).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:336:- Each beam paints teal over bg cells as it moves.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:337:- On hitting an obstacle of color C, consult the legend: bar on left → turn counterclockwise, bar on right → turn clockwise. Continue in the new direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:338:- Beams stop at grid edges.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:339:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:340:Key insight: The legend's bar position (left vs right within its cell) is the encoding for turn direction at each obstacle color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:341:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:342:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:343:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:344:<reference_puzzle index=\"20\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"b9e38dc0\" lines=\"7-18\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:345:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:346:Fill the region enclosed by a wall sprite and radiate color outward through its opening.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:347:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:348:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:349:- bg = most common color. Wall = most frequent non-bg color, forming a partial enclosure (e.g. U-shape).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:350:- A fill-color pixel sits inside the enclosed area. Other non-bg pixels may act as obstacles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:351:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:352:- Flood-fill the enclosed area with the fill color, radiating outward through the wall's open end.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:353:- Obstacles cast \"shadows\" along the radiate direction, blocking fill behind them.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:354:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:355:Key insight: The wall endpoints define the opening direction; fill radiates outward through it, and obstacles block propagation along that same axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:356:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:357:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:358:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:359:你的任务：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:360:以参考题为标杆，运用发散性思维进行创新扩展。请发挥创造力，构思全新且巧妙的推理谜题。用中文创造全新的 ARC 谜题描述。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:361:创新方式包括但不限于：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:362:**机制重组**：将多道参考题各自的核心机制提取出来，组合成一个新的多步管道，用到新的场景。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:363:**机制变异**：取几道参考题的核心机制，以机制为基础进行创新并与其他多种机制进行创新重组，使解题路径发生质变而非量变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:364:**逆向构造**：取一道参考题的输出模式，思考\"什么样的输入规则能产生类似的输出结构但需要完全不同的推理过程\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:365:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:366:严格使用下面的 XML 风格格式输出：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:367:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:368:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:369:- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:370:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:371:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:372:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:373:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:374:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:375:请一次性生成 5 个 `<new_puzzle>`，若有较多合适的创新，也可以生成更多，不设上限，但不要输出额外解释。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:376:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:377:注意事项：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:378:1. 任务不应依赖大量先验知识或复杂计算，而应依赖对模式、结构与空间关系的直觉推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:379:2. 关于\"计算\"的边界：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:380:   - **允许使用**（这些都是人类能心算的视觉量）：数像素 / 孔洞 / 对象 / 邻居（≤10 量级）、比大小、按某个可见属性排序、奇偶判断、取最大 / 最小、用一个计数值作为另一个等量几何量（如 N 个像素 → 长度 N 的射线、面积 N → 边长 N）、判断接触 / 相邻 / 包含、粗略中心位置（簇的视觉中点）、\"距离\"作为\"几步\"而不是公式等人类能够直观感受计算的内容。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:381:   - **禁止使用**（这些是算法量而非视觉量，会迫使解题者依赖公式而非视觉直觉）：曼哈顿 / 欧氏 / Chebyshev 距离作为精确查表键、凸包面积、二进制位编码 / 位运算、模运算（取模） / 余数、拓扑距离（BFS / 最短路 / 跳数）、精确几何质心坐标、凸角 / 凹角计数等复杂且不易被看出来的计算都是禁止使用的。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:382:3. 问题必须能从少量示例中推断出来（通常为 3 对训练样例 + 1 个测试样例）。设计时从人类解题者的视觉角度思考：规则涉及的所有关键要素（对象、关系、属性）必须在网格上肉眼可见，不应依赖人眼无法直接观察到的隐含信息（例如颜色id和颜色亮度是禁止使用的）或需要推算的隐藏属性。规则背后的逻辑本身可以有一定挑战性，但解题所需的所有线索必须能从网格中直接获取。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:383:4. 生成的问题描述旨在促进后续用于创建题目网格的代码生成。因此，对输入 / 输出网格的描述以及规则总结必须极其详细；语言风格应易于理解；对于特定对象（如箭头），必须在描述中明确其绘制方式。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:384:5. 描述谜题时避免使用 0 或 1 这类颜色编号；应使用颜色名称，例如 \"red\"。可用颜色如下：Black、Blue、Red、Green、Yellow、Grey、Magenta、Orange、Azure、Maroon。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:385:6. 5 个新题的核心推理机制应明显不同——即从观察样例到归纳规则的认知路径不同，而不仅仅是场景、对象或颜色不同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:386:7. 题目难度应来自机制的隐蔽性而非步骤数。用参考题作为难度标尺——如果你生成的题一个样例就能猜到规则，说明机制太透明，需要加深隐蔽性。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:387:8. 优先从参考题的机制出发进行重组或推演，而非从物理隐喻出发。物理隐喻容易导致大量题目归结为一种模式，例如\"沿方向移动到阻挡处停止\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:388:9. 题目的难度优先来自规则的**结构层数**，而不是单一步骤的复杂度。关于\"结构层数\"的判定标准：**只有解题者需要主动推理才能完成的步骤才算一层**。肉眼一扫即可获得的信息（如\"找到缺口在哪一侧\"、\"数出像素个数\"、\"识别哪个对象最大\"）不构成独立的推理层——它们只是变换的前置输入，不增加认知难度。真正的多层结构是指每一层都需要解题者发现一个非显然的规律。以两层结构为例：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:389:   - ✗ 伪两层：\"找到缺口方向\"→\"把东西推到对面\" — 第一步肉眼可见，实际只有一层推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:390:   - ✓ 真两层：\"通过孔洞数量匹配颜色图例\"→\"用匹配到的颜色重绘对象\" — 两步都需要非平凡的归纳。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:391:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:392:   如果你发现自己写出的题只是\"对每个对象，根据它的某个属性做某变换\"的单步规则，请引入一个需要主动推理的前置步骤。**用堆叠 tie-break 规则或复杂数学公式来\"加难度\"是劣解；用多一层需要归纳的结构嵌套来\"加难度\"才是好解**。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:393:10. 在符合ARC题目和提示词要求的基础上，鼓励尝试创新规则为多层结构的题目，不局限于两层，可以创新三层或四层结构的题目，但不可为了多结构层数违背要求。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:394:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:395:生成后对生成的题执行以下四项审查（审查内容不需要保存到文件）：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:396:1. 原创性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:397:  新题不可与上述参考题相同或类似，不可只是替换颜色、方向、对象类型等表层要素。判断标准：新题的核心推理路径应与任何一道参考题不同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:398:2. 确定性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/prompt.md:399:  规则完全确定，同一输入只能产生唯一输出，每一步操作都有明确定义。\n/home/lixinyu/